win10xbox: kernelbase exports the entry points the genuine user32/imm32 import through the host API-set map

The guest shares the host PEB, so ApiSetMap is Windows' own schema: api-ms-win-core-heap-obsolete
resolves to kernelbase (Wine: kernel32), and the native user32/imm32 import CheckTokenMembershipEx,
SetProcessValidCallTargets, WTSGetServiceSessionId, WTSIsServerContainer and the Global*/Local* family
from there. Wine had them as stubs or only in kernel32, so the loader bound a stub that raised
EXCEPTION_WINE_STUB (the Global*/Local* ones forward to kernel32).

